inge.", "I am waiting for the kettle to boil, and a teaspoon has slipped down beside the toaster.", "A paperclip slides off the desk and lands on the bare wooden floor with a tiny metallic tick.", "While reaching for a mug, my sleeve catches a cobweb stretched across the kitchen doorway.", "The page of an old paperback unfolds by itself in the evening draft, though the window is closed.", "I found a small battery compartment cover in the junk drawer, but the screws that hold the device open are missing.", "There is a hairline crack in the handle of an otherwise usable ceramic cup.", "A loose button is sitting on the floor near the washing machine, and the machine has just stopped.", "I remember a red bead disappearing from my grandmother's sewing tin, but I cannot recall whether I put it there or found it in my pocket.", "Someone tells me the alarm sounded three times this morning, but I remember only the second one.", "There is a square indentation in the carpet where a toy box used to sit, but I cannot remember when the box was removed.", "I found a note in an old coat pocket saying, “Put it back before she notices,” with no object named.", "A childhood music box sits open on the table, its little cylinder visible but its spring visibly slack.", "A dusty corner contains several screws, and there is a box nearby where I could sort them.", "I tried to open a jammed pencil sharpener by twisting its lid, and now the lid is loose but the blade housing will not turn.", "The strip of tape I used to reseal a cardboard box came loose, and the box split along its old fold.", "I knocked a cup from the counter and it broke, but one triangular shard remains attached by a thin bead of glaze.", "I am brushing crumbs from a sleeve onto the kitchen counter, and one crumb refuses to fall.", "My left shoe lace is shorter than the right, so the knot sits slightly off-center.", "A teaspoon is resting beside the salt shaker, and every time I move the shaker it taps the spoon.", "A friend asks whether the tiny chirping sound from the hallway means something dangerous.", "My cousin says the old toy in my hand is not worth repairing and should be thrown away.", "A cold metal spoon slips from my hand and taps the inside of a ceramic bowl.", "The loose sleeve of an old wool coat brushes a dusty curtain and makes a soft gray puff.", "A tiny bead of honey lands on my thumb while I am opening a jar.", "There is a broken alarm clock on the table, and I could throw it away or take it apart.", "A cardboard box is almost empty, but I have kept every odd piece of packaging inside it.", "I need to answer a message, but one loose plastic screw has rolled into the cuff of my sleeve.", "I tried to remove a battery cover with a coin, and now the cover is scratched and the battery is still inside.", "My attempt to tighten a loose wheel on a toy has stripped the plastic around the axle.", "I tried to wipe up a spill, but the sticky patch has spread and now there are three separate smears near the door.", "I remember a yellow plastic wheel from an old toy box, but not whether it belonged to the red car or the blue truck.", "I remember placing a folded paper in the blue tin yesterday, but when I open the tin there is only dust and one rubber band.", "There is a small notch on the side of the wooden toy horse, and I remember seeing it before, though I cannot remember when.", "I want to explain exactly how the bent clothespin works, but I also want to stop talking and leave it alone.", "I have a clean version of the sentence in my notebook, but the crossed-out draft underneath contains one strange word.", "The dusty corner is nearly clean, but one gray line of dust remains along the baseboard.", "My friend asks why the old toy in my hand keeps making a clicking sound.", "A neighbor asks whether the tapping from the wall means something dangerous.", "I am brushing crumbs from the kitchen counter onto my palm, but one crumb is stuck to the counter.", "A paperclip lies on 