uge across the top disc.", "I tried to flatten a warped cardboard lid with my knee, and now the crease has split and one corner hangs down.", "I cleaned the dusty curtain rail with a cloth, but the dust has now settled in a narrow gray ridge on the floorboards.", "I dropped the toy horse and its head now tilts sideways. I can glue it upright, but I also want to see whether the neck piece is held by a pin.", "I tried to fix the loose wheel on the toy by adding a washer, but the washer is too thick and the wheel will no longer sit flat.", "I remember a yellow bead in the blue tin beside the radio, but when I open the tin there are only two screws and a folded receipt.", "I am pouring tea, and a loose thread on my sweater sleeve has caught the handle of the mug.", "There is a crumb stuck beneath the edge of the kitchen counter label, and I have already wiped the visible surface clean.", "The metal latch on the toolbox is colder than I expect, and my fingertip slides off it the first time.", "A wooden clothes peg snaps shut on the edge of my finger while I am sorting the drawer.", "The corner of the cardboard parcel sleeve brushes my wrist, and the rough paper leaves a warm irritated stripe.", "A bead of cold condensation reaches my wrist while I am carrying the glass across the room.", "The old rattle is beside my chair, and I am supposed to be packing for the move. I could put it in the box now, or open its back and see why the loose bead makes that uneven sound.", "A note on the parcel says, “Return the small blue thing.” I know the drawer is in the next room, but I want to finish reading the note and find out whether the blue thing is even the one being asked for.", "My cousin says the broken music box should go in the bin. It is still on the table, and I have the lid open beside it.", "A friend asks whether the repeated clicking from my desk means the toy is haunted.", "My neighbor asks if the tapping inside the wall could be a pipe problem.", "A tiny screw has rolled under the sofa. There is a ruler beside me, but using it may only push it deeper.", "I cleaned the dusty curtain rail with a brush, and now the dust has settled in a gray pile on the floor beneath it.", "The broken rattle is on the table, and the donation box is open beside it. I could put it in the box, or turn it over and find the loose bead making the uneven beat."]

